stateDiagram-v2
    direction LR
    [*] --> Unset

    Unset: UNSET - no shipped value, behaviour taken from the unset class
    Provisional: PROVISIONAL - a tenant policy or an operator choice recorded with its reason
    Set: SET - a central value with a named setter and a stated basis, still unverified
    Verified: VERIFIED - the value matches a primary source captured with URL and date
    Promoted: PROMOTED - the value now lives as a rule row with its citation, the key kept as an alias
    Superseded: SUPERSEDED - the instrument changed, the alias retired

    Unset --> Provisional: P1 the operator records a choice for one tenant
    Unset --> Set: P2 the statutory lead sets a central value with a basis
    Provisional --> Set: P3 the central value lands and the tenant choice is reconciled
    Set --> Verified: P4 two-person review against the primary source
    Provisional --> Verified: P5 the tenant choice is confirmed by the primary source
    Verified --> Promoted: P6 published as a rule row through the section 22 pipeline
    Promoted --> Superseded: P7 an amendment or corrigendum lands
    Superseded --> Unset: P8 the successor value is unknown, the class applies again
    Set --> Unset: P9 the basis is withdrawn, every dependent artefact re-blocks

    note right of Unset
        no unset parameter may block a pay run for an employee
        blocking is at the artefact or the field, never the person
        counsel-gated keys stay dark even when a value exists
    end note
